    },
    {
      "post_id": "552860641644785666",
      "text": "@joshglancy @johntmarohn I recommend reading the Koran. At the heart of it all violence and murder is allowed for the purpose of converting.",
      "timestamp": "Wed Jan 07 16:13:43 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.5283110798585856e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "553154194459623425",
      "text": ".@NiallODowd @Irish_Fart14 Dunno? Ok. Folks would you like to see a comedy about a man trying to stage a tasteless musical called Springtime",
      "timestamp": "Thu Jan 08 11:40:11 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.529279363248292e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "552838691165839360",
      "text": "HYFR! RT @joshglancy: Rushdie: “Religions, like all other ideas, deserve criticism, satire, and, yes, our fearless disrespect” #CharlieHebdo",
      "timestamp": "Wed Jan 07 14:46:29 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.5283110798585856e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "552869980837257216",
      "text": "@NiallODowd @joshglancy happened today is a different part of the same \"outrage\" wedge that led to calls to stop  the famine sitcom.",
      "timestamp": "Wed Jan 07 16:50:49 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.5286665574403686e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "552866655744036864",
      "text": "@HisEmineminence @joshglancy \nThe famine was not a religion last time I checked",
